  "text": "the roadway environments considered. The practitioner interviews highlighted the benefits of adaptive lighting to the environment but also the need for more details on the implementation of adaptive lighting and support in the industry for system implementation. The surveys of the public highlighted the need for public information. Finally, the on-road assessment experiment highlighted limits to the dimming, with a minimum at 0.45 cd/m2 and a maximum of 0.9 cd/m2. Overall, the energy savings from the dimming system range from 55% initially to 36% at the end of the life of the luminaire system. These results highlight the significant benefits of adaptive lighting without a significant downside. The adaptive approach to lighting should be promoted by the industry and the benefits highlighted. ii Contents 1 Adaptive Lighting for Streets and Residential Areas.............................................................. 1 1.1 Project Goals ................................................................................................................... 1 2 Literature Review .................................................................................................................... 2 2.1 Street Lighting Technology ............................................................................................ 2 2.1.1 Adaptive Lighting ....................................................................................................... 3 2.2 Effects of Street Lighting ................................................................................................ 4 2.2.1 Safety .......................................................................................................................... 4 2.2.2 Security ..................................................................................................................... 13 2.2.3 Environment ........................................................................................................